### API versioning and backward compatibility (unit 5.10)
### Passwords come from .env.

@gatewayUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Login
# @name userLogin
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "demo-user",
  "password": "<DEMO_USER_PASSWORD from .env>"
}

@userToken = {{userLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 2. Versioned path: 200, no Deprecation header.
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products?size=2
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 3. Unversioned path: 200, same body as v1, plus
###   Deprecation: true
###   Link: </api/v1/products>; rel="successor-version"
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/products?size=2
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 4. Unversioned path without a token: 401, exactly like v1.
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/products

### 5. Unknown version: 404 problem+json, nothing forwarded.
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v9/products
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
